opcodes.</li><li>No, because 15 instructions with 3 addresses leave no combinations available for other formats.</li><li>No, because we can only encode a maximum of 15 instructions with 0 addresses.</li></ol>","sourceUrl":"https://www.goclasses.in/","answerSource":{"kind":"learner-provided-screenshot","label":"GO Classes COA Topic Test","capturedAt":"2026-08-13"}}},{"attemptId":"cdfb2e97-1559-4265-b746-b220607ca816","journalQuestionId":"d922f407-f397-4182-a4e7-a45dbe8c695d","reattemptId":"928fb87f-fe71-42ea-a6da-8c8890667f42","questionStartedAt":"2026-08-13T05:28:41.000Z","attemptedAt":"2026-08-13T05:30:33.000Z","scheduledDate":"2026-08-16","timeSpentMs":112000,"number":"2","selectedAnswer":7,"decision":"MARK","markCorrect":false,"timeSpentSec":112,"outcome":"W-C","questionText":"Consider a 68K microprocessor system with a 24-bit address bus ($A_{23}$ to $A_0$) and a 16-bit data bus. The system implements:\nA 1 Mbyte ROM block starting at address $000000_{16}$.\nAn 8 Mbyte DRAM block starting at address $800000_{16}$.\nMemory organization\nROM: 2 sub-blocks × (256K × 16-bit) = 1 Mbyte\nDRAM: 2 banks × 4 parallel (2M × 4-bit) chips = 8 Mbytes\nThe 8 Mbyte DRAM memory block is constructed using multiple $2M \\times 4$-bit memory chips. Because the microprocessor has a 16-bit data bus, multiple 4-bit chips must be arranged in parallel to form a 16-bit word. Calculate the total number of $2M \\times 4$-bit chips required to fully implement this 8 Mbyte DRAM block.","question":{"id":"goclasses:coa-topic-test:2","year":2026,"set":null,"number":"2","paperLabel":"GO Classes COA Topic Test","subject":"Computer Organization","subjectSlug":"coa","classificationHint":{"subjectSlug":"coa","topicSlug":"memory-chip-design"},"topic":"Memory Chip Design","topicSlug":"memory-chip-design","subtopics":["co-and-architecture","memory-chip-design","memory-interfacing","dram","numerical-answers","goclasses-coa-topic-test"],"marks":1,"type":"NAT","answer":8,"tolerance":null,"answerStatus":"available","html":"<p>Consider a 68K microprocessor system with a 24-bit address bus ($A_{23}$ to $A_0$) and a 16-bit data bus. The system implements:</p><ul><li>A 1 Mbyte ROM block starting at address $000000_{16}$.</li><li>An 8 Mbyte DRAM block starting at address $800000_{16}$.</li></ul><pre>Memory organization\nROM:  2 sub-blocks × (256K × 16-bit) = 1 Mbyte\nDRAM: 2 banks × 4 parallel (2M × 4-bit) chips = 8 Mbytes</pre><p>The 8 Mbyte DRAM memory block is constructed using multiple $2M \\times 4$-bit memory chips. Because the microprocessor has a 16-bit data bus, multiple 4-bit chips must be arranged in parallel to form a 16-bit word. Calculate the total number of $2M \\times 4$-bit chips required to fully implement this 8 Mbyte DRAM block.</p>","sourceUrl":"https://www.goclasses.in/","answerSource":{"kind":"learner-provided-screenshot","label":"GO Classes COA Topic Test","capturedAt":"2026-08-13"}}},{"attemptId":"3a942c19-c51a-4dac-ab43-43d1e372d5c5","journalQuestionId":"dffb51a1-7eb2-47b5-bfc4-9dc8e33f78ee","reattemptId":"25d1af5e-fc0a-4f74-9d23-06a232ffbb85","questionStartedAt":"2026-08-13T05:30:38.000Z","attemptedAt":"2026-08-13T05:31:34.000Z","scheduledDate":"2026-08-16","timeSpentMs":56000,"number":"3","selectedAnswer":null,"decision":"SKIP","markCorrect":null,"timeSpentSec":56,"outcome":"W-C","questionText":"Consider a 68K microprocessor system with a 24-bit address bus ($A_{23}$ to $A_0$) and a 16-bit data bus. The system implements:\nA 1 Mbyte ROM block starting at address $000000_{16}$.\nAn 8 Mbyte DRAM block starting at address $800000_{16}$.\nMemory organization\nROM: 2 sub-blocks × (256K × 16-bit) = 1 Mbyte\nDRAM: 2 banks × 4 parallel (2M × 4-bit) chips = 8 Mbytes\nThe 1 Mbyte ROM block starts at base address $000000_{16}$. It is composed of two discrete 512 Kbyte sub-blocks using $256K \\times 16$-bit chips. The microprocessor must use a specific address line to select between the first and second 512 Kbyte sub-blocks. What is the index $k$ of this 